      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1375494983,
      "text": "Colubrina asiatica is a shrub in the family Rhamnaceae that is native to tropical and subtropical regions of the Old World, from eastern Africa to India, southeast Asia, tropical Australia, and the Pacific Islands. Common names include latherleaf, Asian nakedwood, Asian snakewood, and ʻĀnapanapa (Hawaii)."
    }
